        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Fred Gehrke, Christian Yelich\n- Organizations: Los Angeles Rams, Miami Marlins\n- Events: 1948 Los Angeles Rams season, 2010 Major League Baseball Draft\n- Concepts: first helmet logo in league history, family relationship\n\nFacts:\n- In 1948, the Los Angeles Rams debuted the first helmet logo in league history.\n- In 1948, Los Angeles Rams running back Fred Gehrke conceived the idea for the team's helmet logo.\n- In 2010, the Miami Marlins drafted Christian Yelich out of high school in the first round with the 23rd overall pick of the Major League Baseball Draft.\n- Fred Gehrke is the great-grandfather of Miami Marlins player Christian Yelich.",
